    {
      "kind": "page",
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Race conditions and synchronization",
      "images": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Race conditions and synchronization",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "What just happened is called a race condition",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Concurrent execution can lead to different results",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Critical section: portion of code that can lead to race conditions",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "What we need: mutual exclusion",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "Only one thread should be executing critical section at any time",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "What we need: atomicity of the critical section",
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "The critical section should execute like one uninterruptible instruction",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "list_item",
          "text": "How is it achieved? Locks (topic of next lecture)",
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
